WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.269
-There is no sign
that the government shutdown

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.537
will end any time soon,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.139
and now the president wants
a primetime address

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:08.708
to repeat his lies.
For more on this,

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.343
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:11.878
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.914 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:17.617
-Our political system feels like
it's at a breaking point.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:20.019
It was always fragile,
but then Donald Trump

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.154
came along and wrecked it.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:22.989
He's like the guy at a party

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.357
watching a game of "Jenga,"

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.826
going [ As Trump ]
"Take that one! No, that one!"

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.227
[ Normal voice ]
And then finally, someone says,

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:29.829
"You know what -- if you think
it's so easy, you try it."

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.664
And then he just lights
the "Jenga" tower on fire.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.932
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.934
[ As Trump ] Boom, now I collect
the insurance money,

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.403
build a bigger tower.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.071
[ Normal voice ]
There is no more basic test

00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:40.440
of a political leader
than this --

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.709
Can you keep the government
running?

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.911
And Trump is now again
failing that test

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.779
for the third time
in his presidency.

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:49.482
In real life, you don't
get rehired after that.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:52.385
He's like a stoner
working at a pizza place.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.420
"Hey, Kevin,
how was business today?"

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.990
"Oh, yeah,
it was really slow, man."

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.359
"Did you unlock the front door?"

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.759
"Ohhhhh, maaan!"

00:01:00.759 --> 00:01:02.762
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.164
"I'm sorry, Kevin.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:08.868
You have given me no choice,
Kevin

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.271
You're going to get
the Cecil B. DeMille award."

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:13.072
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:16.175
And the government shutdown
that is now in its third week

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.678
isn't just a political fight
over a useless border wall

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:21.247
that Trump repeatedly said
Mexico would pay for.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.849
It's having real world
consequences

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.717
for millions of people
from federal workers

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.520
going without pay to anyone
who flies on an airplane.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.558
-15 Federal Agencies
are affected by the shutdown.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:35.995
420,000 federal employees
are working without pay,

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:40.266
and 380,000 employees
are now on unpaid leave.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.902
-Federal Tax refunds
will be delayed.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:46.105
Food stamps for 38-million
Americans will be cut.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:49.141
Millions of people will lose
rental assistance payments,

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:52.278
and union leaders say hundreds
of TSA workers

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.246
are already off the job.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:57.149
-Already hundreds of TSA
employees have missed work

00:01:57.149 --> 00:01:58.918
at major airports
across the country.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.454
It's fueling concerns
of possible security risks

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.988
and travel disruptions.

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.191
-Can you imagine
what a nightmare that'll be?

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.161
It's a major disruption
when one TSA agent

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.129
has to go get more plastic bins.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:11.397
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.433
Think about that -- Donald Trump
is such a bad president,

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.401
he found a way to
make air travel worse

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:16.969
than it already was.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:19.405
By the end of his term, the only
airline will be Spirit.

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:21.708
The only in-flight movie
will be "Dirty Grandpa,"

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.810
and every seat will be
a middle seat.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.880
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:34.487
We are a self-inflicted crisis
over a government shutdown

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.923
because the president is
incompetent and unhinged.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.291
He's virtually incapable
of uttering

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.694
a truthful or coherent thought
about almost anything.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.931
Just take one of the most basic
responsibilities of his job --

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:46.032
national security.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:47.467
Here's Trump from last week

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.868
describing a meeting with
generals at the Pentagon

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:50.970
who tried to brief him

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.805
on dangerous spots
around the world.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.173
-When I became president,

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:57.844
I had a meeting at the Pentagon
with lots of generals.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.445
They were like from a movie.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.014
Better looking than Tom Cruise
and stronger.

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:03.215
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:05.318
And I had more generals
than I've ever seen.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:08.688
And we were at the bottom
of this incredible room.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.490
I said, this is the greatest
room I've ever seen.

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.762
I saw more computer boards than
I think that they make today.

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.797
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:21.433
-Why -- why does he always
sound like a co-worker

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:23.403
telling you about a dream
he had?

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:24.636
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.636 --> 00:03:26.639
[ As Trump ] There were --
There were generals,

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.775
and we were in this room
with computer boards, right?

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.578
And you were there,
but you weren't you. You know?

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.246
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:35.982
You had your head, but my body!

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.983
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.983 --> 00:03:39.352
[ Normal voice ]
At that same meeting,

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:42.121
Trump rattled off a bizarre
and incoherent explanation

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.224
of the Russian invasion
of Afghanistan in 1979.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.860
Now the Soviet occupation
of Afghanistan was condemned

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.229
at the time and since.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.929
Only Russia
has tried to justify it

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:53.499
until last week, when the
president of the United States

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.002
publicly stated for the first
time that Russia was right

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.104
to invade and occupy
Afghanistan.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.606
-Russia used to be
the Soviet Union.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.674
Afghanistan made it Russia,

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:06.812
because they went bankrupt
fighting in Afghanistan.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:11.617
Russia. The reason Russia
was in Afghanistan

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.454
was because terrorists
were going into Russia.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.055
They were right to be there.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.657
The problem is
it was a tough fight.

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:20.392
And literally
they went bankrupt.

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:23.362
They went into being
called Russia again,

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:25.164
as opposed to the Soviet Union.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:28.601
-Look, sometimes you get
involved in something

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.903
that goes so badly,
you have to change your name.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:34.106
For example, you take a job
as Donald J. Trump,

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:36.442
and you leave it
as Prisoner 567891.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.644
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:42.782
Although, let's be honest.
Let's be honest.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.418
Best outcome,
Trump cooperates with Mueller,

00:04:45.418 --> 00:04:48.421
rolls on everyone else, and goes
into witness protection.

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:51.023
[ As Trump ] Hi, I'm your
new neighbor, Ronald Bump.

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:55.694
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.694 --> 00:04:57.529
I don't want to say
why I moved here,

00:04:57.529 --> 00:04:59.098
but it was Obama's fault.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:00.499
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.499 --> 00:05:01.801
[ Normal voice ] Also,
I love how Trump thinks

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.702
it's an amazing insight

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:06.906
to say Russia used to be
the Soviet Union.

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.942
He thought it was so impressive,
he said it twice.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.978
-Russia used to be
the Soviet Union.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:14.947
They went into being called
Russia again,

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.782
as opposed to the Soviet Union.

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:21.320
-Wow! Really, Dr. History?

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.023
Russia used to be
the Soviet Union?

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.724
This sounds like
when the gym teacher

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:28.460
has to cover social studies
for a week.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.330
All right. All right, everybody,
settle down!

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.266
We're going to watch "Red Dawn."

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:36.068
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:38.070
And that was nothing
compared to the stream

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.673
of incoherent nonsense Trump
reeled off at a press conference

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:42.641
at the White House on Friday
after a meeting

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:44.310
with Congressional leaders
on the shutdown.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.211
The press conference got crazier
as it went on,

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:48.681
including a point in which Trump
tried incoherently

00:05:48.681 --> 00:05:51.584
to explain how migrants
cross the Southern border.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.820
-We've already built
a lot of the wall.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.154
We have renovated
a tremendous amount of wall.

00:05:56.154 --> 00:05:58.991
I just told you, we did
a lot of wall in San Diego.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:02.027
Steel is stronger than concrete.

00:06:02.027 --> 00:06:04.363
So if I have a steel wall

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:06.799
or you could call it
a steel fence --

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:09.335
We're not talking about games.

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.570
And I called up.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:13.372
I said, "Hi,
it's President Trump.

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:15.241
What's going on?"
They said, "President Trump,

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.375
we don't know who that is."

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:19.344
They come in through these vast,
open areas.

00:06:19.344 --> 00:06:21.313
They get off the road,

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:23.416
and they drive out
into the desert,

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.251
and they come in,
they make a left turn.

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:26.953
Usually it's a left,
not a right.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:29.555
These coyotes
and these human traffickers,

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:34.093
they make a right turn before
they get to the port of entry.

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:39.164
They go as far as the wall is,
or as far as the barricade is,

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:41.767
and then they make a left.

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.504
Welcome to the United States.

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:47.339
-The coyotes drive
across the border,

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:49.909
they make a right, then a left,
they go as far as the wall,

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.344
and then it's welcome
to the United States.

00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:54.213
That idea is so insane
and incoherent,

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:57.249
there's a good chance he got it
from watching cartoons.

00:06:57.249 --> 00:06:59.418
[ As Trump ] These coyotes,
they're strapping themselves

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:02.889
to rockets and shooting
themselves over the border,

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:06.158
so we have to build a wall and
we have to paint a tunnel on it.

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:10.096
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.096 --> 00:07:11.797
That's how you get 'em,
with the tunnel.

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:15.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
You get 'em with the tunnel.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:17.870
[ Normal voice ] Trump started
out the press conference

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.705
by inviting Congressional
leaders to speak,

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.907
and just to give an idea
of how fried his brain is,

00:07:21.907 --> 00:07:24.176
watch how he thanks house
Republican minority leader

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:25.911
Kevin McCarthy
after his comments.

00:07:25.911 --> 00:07:29.014
Once again,
this is Kevin McCarthy speaking.

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:31.584
-We will stay in the room
and get this job done.

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:34.620
And there was progress today.
I look forward to solving it.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.555
-Thank you, Steve.
-I mean...

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:38.057
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:39.724
Now, now...

00:07:39.724 --> 00:07:41.860
in fairness to Trump,

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.629
if you forget
an old white guy's name,

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.798
you have a decent chance if you
just throw out a Steve.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.533
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:49.635
But maybe the wildest thing
Steve said on --

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:50.703
[ Chuckles ] Steve.

00:07:50.703 --> 00:07:52.438
[ Laughter ]

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.173
[Bleep] this guy.

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.075
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:58.010
This guy. [Bleep]

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:01.147
Hey! Hey, you got
a glass house over there?!

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:03.716
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.257
Oh, it's good to be back.

00:08:11.257 --> 00:08:13.192
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:15.427
But maybe the wildest thing
Trump said on Friday

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:18.163
was when he threatened to start
building the wall unilaterally

00:08:18.163 --> 00:08:20.232
by declaring
a national emergency.

00:08:20.232 --> 00:08:23.502
-Have you considered
using emergency powers

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:25.904
to grant yourself authorities
to build this wall

00:08:25.904 --> 00:08:29.241
without Congressional approval?
And second --

00:08:29.241 --> 00:08:30.576
-Yes, I have.
-You have?

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.811
-Yes, I have.
And I can do it if I want.

00:08:32.811 --> 00:08:35.047
-So you don't need Congressional
approval to build the wall?

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:36.749
-No, we can use them --
absolutely.

00:08:36.749 --> 00:08:38.416
We can call a national emergency

00:08:38.416 --> 00:08:41.253
because of the security
of our country, absolutely.

00:08:41.253 --> 00:08:42.721
No, we can do it.
I haven't done it.

00:08:42.721 --> 00:08:44.890
I may do it. I may do it.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:47.125
But we could call
a national emergency

00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:48.727
and build it very quickly.

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:50.930
-Just a side note here --
reporters,

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.065
stop asking questions like that.

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.601
There's a good chance that Trump

00:08:55.601 --> 00:08:57.970
never thought about using
emergency power

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.838
until that reporter
brought it up.

00:08:59.838 --> 00:09:02.674
He is very suggestible.
A reporter could say,

00:09:02.674 --> 00:09:04.610
"Mr. President,
have you thought about wearing

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:07.346
a military uniform everywhere
and executing your enemies

00:09:07.346 --> 00:09:08.714
in the rose garden?"
And he would go,

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.383
[ As Trump ] "We're looking
into that very strongly.

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:13.386
Did you get that?
Write that down, I like that."

00:09:13.386 --> 00:09:15.287
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:16.622
[ Normal voice ]
Apparently, that performance

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.357
wasn't crazy enough,
because today Trump announced

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:20.392
he wants to address the nation
on Tuesday night,

00:09:20.392 --> 00:09:23.362
and even in his tweet announcing
the speech, Trump lied.

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.665
He tweeted, "I'm pleased to
inform you that I will address

00:09:25.665 --> 00:09:28.100
the nation on the humanitarian
and national security crisis

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.903
on our Southern border Tuesday
night at 9:00 P.M. Eastern."

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:33.105
Okay, first of all, just because
Trump wants to address

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:35.841
the nation doesn't mean networks
should air it.

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:38.611
Otherwise they're just passing
on his lies unfiltered.

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:40.913
They should either
reject him outright,

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:43.916
or if he insists on speaking
in primetime,

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:47.953
make him do it as a contestant
on "The Masked Singer."

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:50.055
-They get off the road,

00:09:50.055 --> 00:09:52.591
and they drive out into the
desert and they come in,

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:53.859
they make a left turn.

00:09:53.859 --> 00:09:55.294
Usually it's a left,
not a right.

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:57.429
[ Laughter ]
-Second...

00:09:57.429 --> 00:09:59.665
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:06.805
...there's no national security
crisis at the border.

00:10:06.805 --> 00:10:09.241
Trump and his aides
keep repeating the debunked lie

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:11.510
that terrorists are sneaking in
from Mexico.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.345
Yesterday,
Sarah Huckabee Sanders tried it

00:10:13.345 --> 00:10:15.680
